#' with \eqn{h = 1 + (n - 1) p}, \eqn{l = \lfloor h \rfloor},
#' and \eqn{u = \lceil h \rceil},
#' the quantile is \eqn{(1 - (h - l)) x_{(l)} + (h - l) x_{(u)}},
#' or \eqn{x_{(l)}} when \eqn{h = l} or \eqn{x_{(u)} = x_{(l)}}.
#' `x` has no missing values (the callers drop them).
